/-! ## §3b — the welds, now that the objects exist. -/

/-- ⚑ **THE WELD to the proof↔proof chain gate.** The commitment half of word 12's preimage IS the
accumulator `PicklesProofChainGate.linkOk` compares against the parent block's own `sg`, and the
raw prechallenges ARE the ones it compares against the parent's own 16. So word 12 does not merely
commit the served header — it commits the header TOGETHER WITH this proof's position in the chain,
and the two gates are about one object rather than sitting beside one another. -/
theorem word12_preimage_carries_the_chain_accumulator :
    (B539795.accComm.take 2 = [PicklesProofChainGate.B539795.accX,
                               PicklesProofChainGate.B539795.accY]
     ∧ B539795.accChals.take 16 = PicklesProofChainGate.B539795.accCh)
    ∧ (B539796.accComm.take 2 = [PicklesProofChainGate.B539796.accX,
                                 PicklesProofChainGate.B539796.accY]
     ∧ B539796.accChals.take 16 = PicklesProofChainGate.B539796.accCh)
    ∧ (B539797.accComm.take 2 = [PicklesProofChainGate.B539797.accX,
                                 PicklesProofChainGate.B539797.accY]
     ∧ B539797.accChals.take 16 = PicklesProofChainGate.B539797.accCh) := by
  refine ⟨⟨?_, ?_⟩, ⟨?_, ?_⟩, ⟨?_, ?_⟩⟩ <;> decide

/-- …and the chain gate ACCEPTS that run, so the weld's premise is nonempty: these are three
genuinely consecutive blocks, and word 12 of each is the digest of its own served header over its
genuinely-adjacent parent's accumulator. -/
theorem the_welded_run_chains :
    PicklesProofChainGate.chainOk
      [PicklesProofChainGate.B539795, PicklesProofChainGate.B539796,
       PicklesProofChainGate.B539797] = true := by decide

